<!--
  SYNTHETIC F9 FIXTURE. Not JLR evidence and not promotable to evidence.

  Reproduces only the element shape of an SDD IVS part-lineage document
  (COMMON_JLR_SMPACK_XML/IVS). Values exercise parsing branches:

    * an assembly declared twice, once per node, whose parts are gathered;
    * a supporting software part with no identifier, and one whose
      identifier is SDD's own `SECX` rather than four hex digits: neither
      can be compared with anything a module answers, so neither is
      recorded;
    * a lineage with no parts at all;
    * a second module, so a lookup has to pick the right one.

  The programming attributes of a lineage block are present and ignored on
  purpose: ADR-0033 records numbers, never instructions.
-->
